// libGaugeApp.so - an iDrive-7-style engine screen (coolant / oil temperature, g-meter, gear, power, torque, all-time
// maxima) as a native iDrive "PluginApp" for BMW NBT Evo (ID5 / ID6) and EntryNav2 head units.
//
// How it works: HmiMain3D loads Plugins/GaugeApp/GaugeApp.manifest at boot. GaugeApp.xml (generated by make_db.py)
// adds a menu row and one screen (hmiState 10): a background image and image components on top of it, each bound to
// a raImageModel. This library loads every frame from GaugeApp_frames.bin, subscribes to the car's CDS properties (the
// call NBT-AAD / entry-aad use for driving.gear), keeps the latest values and, five times a second, sends the PNG data
// of every image whose picture changed with PluginApp::updateModel(model, bmw::Image) - arc / marker frames, digits,
// the g-meter dot, the gear cells (src/gauge_view.hpp decides which). The frames are not in the HMI's image DB: with
// all of them there, an EntryNav2 showed no image at all (see make_db.py). The maxima start from nothing every time
// the app starts; those of the last run are kept in <data dir>/max.txt.
//
// The framework glue (PluginApp constructor, own vtable, Runnable stand-in, pluginAppInfo) is the pattern car-verified
// by NBT-AAD's rhmiapp/nbt_aad_app.cpp (https://github.com/Sq00ky/Supra-iDrive6-Android-Auto) and entry-aad's
// hmiapp/bmw_framework.cpp; only the declarations that are needed here are repeated, there are no BMW headers.
//
// Two targets are built from this one file:
//   NBT Evo (default)     QNX 6.5, qcc / GCC 4.4, installed in /opt/hmi/ID5/data/ro/Plugins/GaugeApp
//   EntryNav2 (-DGAUGE_ENTRYNAV2)  EntryEVO, Linux ARMv7 hard-float, glibc 2.15, installed in
//                         /opt/hmi/data/ro/Plugins/GaugeApp; differences are in the "platform" blocks below.
//
// Logs: NBT Evo slog (code 0x4e47); EntryNav2 <data dir>/gauge-app.log; both also <usb stick>/gauge-app.log if that
// file already exists on a stick (create an empty one on a PC to switch it on).
